  $kt$["Botox is priced per unit at ₦12,000, so the cost depends on how much muscle you're treating, not on a flat fee.","Nothing happens for the first three days. Movement softens over about a week and settles by day fourteen.","Results last three to four months. Nobody's first treatment is their best one — dosing gets refined the second time.","It relaxes muscle, so it treats lines that appear when you move. Lines visible on a still face need a different treatment.","Botulinum toxin is prescription-only. The person injecting you should be a licensed medical professional who can manage a complication."]$kt$::jsonb,
  $faq$[{"question":"How much does Botox cost in Lagos?","answer":"At Reverse Aesthetics, Botox is ₦12,000 per unit, so the final price depends on how many units your muscles need. Common treatment areas are priced whole: a lip flip is ₦120,000, a brow lift ₦45,000, gummy smile correction ₦200,000, and masseter slimming for jaw width or grinding is ₦300,000."},{"question":"How long does Botox take to work?","answer":"You won't see anything for about three days. Movement starts softening between days three and seven, and the full result is there at two weeks. Any review or top-up should wait until day fourteen, because judging the result before then leads to overtreatment."},{"question":"How long does Botox last?","answer":"Three to four months for most people. Strong muscles, a fast metabolism, and heavy exercise all shorten it. The muscle recovers gradually rather than switching back on, so movement returns over a few weeks."},{"question":"Does Botox hurt?","answer":"The needle is very fine and each injection takes a second or two. Most people describe a brief sting. No anaesthetic is needed for standard areas, and the whole appointment takes about fifteen minutes."},{"question":"Will Botox make my face look frozen?","answer":"That comes from dose and placement, not from the drug. Too much in the forehead removes movement entirely and can drop the brow. A conservative first dose, reviewed at two weeks and adjusted, is how you avoid it. You can always add more; you cannot take it away."},{"question":"Can I get Botox while pregnant or breastfeeding?","answer":"No. It isn't given during pregnancy or breastfeeding. Tell your injector if you're pregnant, trying to conceive, breastfeeding, take muscle relaxants or certain antibiotics, or have a neuromuscular condition such as myasthenia gravis."}]$faq$::jsonb,
  'Botox in Lagos: Cost, Results & What to Expect | Reverse Aesthetics', 'Botox in Lagos costs from ₦12,000 per unit. How it works, what each area costs, how long it lasts, and how to pick a safe injector.'
